NATIONALLAS ST' MBLY SECRBTARIATORDERS OF THE DAY
for the meeting of the National Assembly to be held on Tuesday, the l3th January, 2026 at I I :00 a'm
Tilawat, Hadith, I',iaat and national anthem.CALLING ATTENTION NOTICE
2, SYED NAVEED QAMAR DR. SHARMILA FARUQUIMR. ABDUL QADIR PATEL SYED RAF'ITILLAHMIR GHULAM ALI TALPIR to invite attention of the Minister for Planning, Developmentand Special Initiatives to a matter of urgent public importance regarding federal takeover of the Rs. 465billion Lahore-Bahawalnagar motorway project in violation of federal fiscal dues and diversion of resourcesfrom nationally strategic projects, causing grave concern amongst the public.
INTRODUCTION OF BILLS3. DR. SHARMILA FARUQUI to move for leave to introduce a Bill further to amend theNational Database and Registration Authority Ordinance, 2000 [The National Database and RegistrationAuthority (Amendmen| Bill, 20251.4. Also to introduce the Bill, if leave is granted.5. MS. SEHAR KAMRANSHAZIA MARRI to move for leave to introduce a Bill further to provide forenvironmentally sound management of lifecycle of batteries, prevent environmentalpollution, protegt publichealth, and promote a circular economy [The ICT Bafferies (Management and Recycling) Bill, 2025].6. Also to introduce the Bill, if leave is granted'
7. MR. TAHIR IQBAL to move for leave to introduce a Bill further to amend the Co-operativeSocieties Act,1925 [The Co-operative Societies (Amendment) Bill, 2025].8. Also to introduce the Bill, if leave is granted.PRESENTATION OF PERIODICAL REPORTS OF THE STANDING COMMITTEEg. MR. MUHAMMAD JAWED HANIF KHAN, Chairman Standing Committee on Commerce, topresent the Periodical Report of the Committee for the period l" January, 2025 to 30th June, 2025, asiequired by rule 234-Aof the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the National Assembly, 2007.10. MALIK MSHAMMAD AAMIR DOGAR, Chairman Standing Committee on Religious Affairsand lnterfaith Harmony, to present the Periodical Report of the Committee for the period I't January, 2025to 30fi June,2025, as required by rule 234-A of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in theNational Assembly, 2007.11. MS. ZAHRA WADOOD FATEMI, Chairperson Standing Committee on Human Rights, to presentthe Periodical Report of the Committee for the period I't January, 2025 to 30'n June, 2025, as required byrule 234-Aof the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the National Assembly, 2007.lZ. MS. MUNAZA HASSAN, Chairperson Standing Commiffee on Climate Change andEnvironmental Coordination, to present the Periodical Report of tn. Committee for the period l't January,2025 to 30ft June, 2025, as required by rule 234-A of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in theNational Assembly, 2007.13. SYED ABDUL QADIR GILANI, Chairman Standing Committee on Planning, Development andSpecial Initiatives to present the Periodical Report of the Comirittee for the period l" Jinuary, 2025 to 30hline,2025, as requirid by rule 234-A of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in the NationalAssembly,2007.

