MOTION14. RAJA KHURRAM SIIAHZAD NAWAZ, Chairman Standing Committee on Interior andNarcotics Control to move that the delay in the presentation of report of the Standing Committee on the Billfurther to amend the Capital Development Authority Ordinance, 1960 [The Capital Development Authority(Amendment) Bill, 2025), till today be condoned. (Moved by Shazia Marri, MNA).PRESENTATION OF REPORT OF THE STANDING COMMITTEE15. RAJA KHURRAM SHAHZAD NAWAZ, Chairman Standing Committee on Interior andNarcotics Control to present the report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amend the CapitalDevelopment Authority Ordinance, 1960 [The Capital Development Authority (Arnendment) Bill, 2025).
MOTION16. SYED NAVEED QAMAR, Chairman Standing Committee on Finance and Revenue to move thatthe delay in the presentation of report of the Standing Committee on the Bill to provide for the CorporateSocial Responsibility in Profit-making Companies [The Corporate Social Responsibility Bill, 2025), tilltoday be condoned. (Moved by Dr. Nafisa Shah, MNA).PRESENTATION OT REPORT OF'THE STANDING COMMITTEE17. SYED NAVEED QAMAR, Chairman Standing Committee on Finance and Revenue to present thereport of the Standing Committee on the Bill to provide for the Corporate Social Responsibility in Profit-making Companies [The Corporate Social Responsibility Bill, 20251.MOTION18. DR. SHAZIA SOBIA ASLAM SOOMRO, Acting Chairperson Standing Commiffee on FederalEducation and Professional Training to move that the delay in the presentation of report of the StandingCommittee on the Bill to provide for the establishment of Allied Institute at Multan [The Allied Institute,Multan Bill,2025l, till today be condoned. (Moved by Khawaja Izhar Ul Hassan, MNA).PRESENTATION OF REPORT OF THE STAI\DING COMMITTEE19. DR. SHAZIA SOBIA ASLAM SOOMRO, Acting Chairperson Standing Committee on FederalEducation and Professional Training to present the report of the Standing Committee on the Bill to providefor the establishment of Allied Institute at Multan [The Allied Institute, Multan Bill,2025].RESOLUTION20. SYED RAFIULLAH to move the following resolution:-
"This House is of the opinion that the Government should take immediate steps to investigate theoff-loading of documented passengers at various airports and recommend the administrative reformsto ensure transparency, accountability, and the protection of passenger rights, while improvingcommunication so that all off-loading decisions are lawful and properly documented.o'
21.
MATTERS OTHER TIIAN POINTS OF'ORDERRaising matters under Rule 18 which are not Points of Order.CALLING ATTENTION NOTICE
22. MR. MUHAMMAD RIAZ FATYANA to invite attention of the Minister for Interior andNarcotics Control, to a matter of urgent public importance regarding wanton tree cutting in Islamabad,causing grave concern amongst the public.
Islamabad, the12th January. 2026
SAE,E,D AHMAD MAITLAActing Secretary

